"""47-minute introduction. The separate workshop owns the three worked cases."""
SLIDES=[]
def add(title, points=(), *, minutes=1.5, refs=(), image=None, image2=None, caption='', caption2='', table=None, kind='normal', note='', takeaway=''):
    SLIDES.append(dict(title=title,points=list(points),minutes=minutes,refs=list(refs),image=image,image2=image2,caption=caption,caption2=caption2,table=table,kind=kind,note=note,takeaway=takeaway))

add('Agentic AI for Utility Operators', ['Motivation, frameworks and evidence','Introduction before the three-use-case workshop','45–50 minutes · Evidence reviewed 17 October 2026'],minutes=.5,refs=['B01'],kind='cover',note='Introduce the session as the motivation and vocabulary tutorial. Worked voltage, restoration and cyber-response experiments belong to the next workshop. This is an independent educational adaptation of the IEEE ComSoc theme.')
add('The route for this session',table=[['Part','Question','Minutes'],['Operator context','Why might agents help?','8'],['Agent foundations','What makes a system agentic?','10'],['Company evidence','What is actually reported?','6.5'],['Frameworks and research','What can we reuse?','14.5'],['Motivation and discussion','What will the next tutorial test?','8']],minutes=1, note='The speaker schedule totals 47 minutes, including discussion. The table groups the material approximately; use the precise cumulative times in the instructor guide. Keep the source guide available for reading after the talk.',takeaway='Today: understand the pattern. Next session: work through the three cases.')
add('Inside the control room', ['PJM’s operating team covers the grid 24 hours a day, seven days a week.','Operators balance supply and demand, watch overloads and prepare for changing weather.','Duke’s 2022 profile describes one operator using a dozen monitors.'],image='duke_control_room.jpg',caption='Duke Energy control room, 2022. Photograph used for operating context.',minutes=1.5,refs=['O01','I02'],note='Team coverage is not an individual shift length. The monitor count is one historical operator profile. Ask the audience which displays they consult to understand an event.',takeaway='The decision depends on several sources of evidence.')
add('A changing planning envelope', ['PJM’s January 2026 forecast projects 3.6% average annual summer-peak growth over ten years.','The same report uses 403 weather scenarios. These are planning inputs, not a count of an operator’s daily tasks.'],image='framework_pjm_summer_peak.png',caption='Original PJM forecast chart, printed report p. 9. MW; forecast vintages are labeled.',kind='figure',minutes=2,refs=['M01'],note='Point to the two forecast vintages and their different trajectories. These are forecasts, not observed future demand. The teaching inference is a need to track changing assumptions and evidence; this chart does not prove an agent’s benefit.',takeaway='An agent must preserve the date, assumptions and provenance of an analysis.')
add('Control-room responsibilities',table=[['PJM example','Responsibility','Possible assistant support'],['Generation Dispatcher','Balance and reserves','Summarize changes and exceptions'],['Power Dispatcher','Transmission security; outages; voltage','Assemble asset and outage evidence'],['Reliability Engineer','Next-day outage studies','Explain approved study results'],['Shift Supervisor / Master Coordinator','Shift leadership / forecasts and interchange','Prepare coordinated briefings']],minutes=1.5,refs=['O02'],note='These are PJM positions; the last row groups two distinct desks for brevity. The bulletin says positions do not map one-to-one onto NERC functional titles. Suggested assistant support is a teaching proposal.',takeaway='Assign a task to a desk and a named decision owner.')
add('Operators already use specialized tools', ['CAISO describes wildfire maps with transmission overlays and camera views.','Its reported Real-Time Contingency Analysis cycle is every five minutes.','The opportunity is to connect these outputs with procedures and the current task.'],image='caiso_watch_duty.png',caption='Actual Watch Duty screenshot published by California ISO, 2025.',minutes=1.5,refs=['O05'],note='This is existing situational-awareness software. Five minutes describes the reported RTCA analysis cycle, not an AI response-time guarantee. A proposed agent would organize evidence around these established tools.',takeaway='An agent coordinates tools around an operator’s question.')
add('Assistant, agent and automatic controller',table=[['System','What it does','Example'],['Assistant','Produces an answer from a request','Retrieve an approved procedure'],['Agent','Chooses tools, keeps state and responds to results','Gather evidence, request a study, revise a plan'],['Automatic controller','Executes a specified control strategy','Protection or voltage-control function']],minutes=2,refs=['T01'],note='Use these as teaching definitions. A conventional controller may be highly automated without an LLM. An agent can mix deterministic application steps and model choices.',takeaway='Agentic behavior is about a goal-directed process with tool feedback.')
add('Workflow or agent?', ['A workflow follows specified routes. An agent can choose its next action from the observed result.'],image='framework_langgraph_workflow.png',caption='Original LangGraph documentation comparison of workflow patterns and agents.',kind='figure',minutes=2,refs=['T01','V01'],note='Point to the left-hand predefined paths, then the right-hand tool/feedback loop. A useful application often combines both: agent choices inside a bounded workflow. Do not walk through every mini-diagram.',takeaway='Keep predictable checks explicit; use an agent where task choices vary.')
add('The components behind an operator assistant',table=[['Component','Purpose','Observable evidence'],['Model','Interpret the goal and propose a next step','Proposed tool request'],['Retrieval','Find approved documents and records','Source and revision'],['Tools','Read data or perform a calculation','Arguments and returned result'],['State','Track the case across steps','Case ID, timestamp, topology version'],['Checks and review','Decide whether the result is usable','Passed checks, gaps, reviewer decision']],minutes=1.5,refs=['T01','T02'],note='These components describe a proposed teaching architecture. The model does not replace the calculator or simulator. Show the audience what can be inspected rather than discussing hidden model reasoning.',takeaway='A fluent answer is only one output of the whole system.')
add('MCP and A2A connect different things',table=[['Interface','Connects','Utility teaching example'],['MCP','An application to tools and context','A governed historian or procedure reader'],['A2A','Independent agents exchanging tasks and results','Ask a separately managed asset-analysis agent'],['Application policy','Identity, permissions and allowed actions','Decide which case and tool a user may access']],minutes=1.5,refs=['T08','T09','T10'],note='Protocols make systems interoperable. They do not establish electrical feasibility or grant a tool permission by themselves. The third row is a separate application responsibility, not a third agent protocol.',takeaway='Connectivity and authority are separate design questions.')
add('One useful operator request', ['“Summarize open alarms and changes since the previous shift. Cite the records; draft only.”','The assistant reads the event log and relevant historian data.','It returns open items with status, time, owner and evidence links.','The incoming operator reconciles the brief with the official log and outgoing operator.'],image='duke_operator.jpg',caption='Duke Energy operator photograph. The request shown is illustrative.',minutes=1.5,refs=['I03'],note='This is an illustrative interaction rather than a disclosed Duke agent feature. A missing log or conflicting timestamp should be returned as a gap. Leave the full prompt, permissions and tool-contract exercise to the next session.',takeaway='The first useful output can be a better briefing, with sources attached.')
add('Authority must be explicit',table=[['Task level','Agent output','Decision boundary'],['Read','Source-linked summary','Approved evidence access'],['Recommend','Options plus study results','Operator reviews feasibility'],['Prepare','Draft plan or work item','Named reviewer approves'],['Execute','An authorized action request','Separate service enforces permission']],minutes=1.5,note='This ladder is a proposed teaching aid, not an industry standard. Existing operating procedures and control responsibilities determine the permitted action. Explain this boundary once here and carry it into the examples.',takeaway='The application must enforce the boundary described to the user.')
add('CAISO: a real operator-assistance case', ['CAISO described a RAG and multi-agent pilot for planned-outage review in 2025.','OATI’s 2026 field report describes production use with reviewers retaining the decision.','OATI reports a nightly batch of 500+ next-day requests processed in under eight minutes.'],image='caiso_control_room.jpg',caption='California ISO control room, published by OATI. Context photograph.',minutes=2,refs=['C01','C02','I06'],note='The pilot is described by CAISO; the production status and timing are supplier-reported. The metric measures review throughput. It does not independently establish a reduction in outage risk or autonomous switching.',takeaway='Evidence assembly and screening can fit an existing reviewed workflow.')
add('GE: operational foundation and agentic application',image='ge_gridos_control_room.jpg',caption='GE Vernova GridOS promotional composite. Alabama Power is a named early adopter.',image2='ge_aerospace_services.jpg',caption2='GE Aerospace services photograph from its AI overview.',kind='pair',table=[['Business','Disclosed work','Evidence meaning'],['GE Vernova','GridOS distribution orchestration','A trusted operations foundation; LLM agency not established'],['GE Aerospace','Selected supply-chain tasks using Palantir AIP','Explicit company-reported agentic deployment']],minutes=1.5,refs=['C07','C05','I01','I07'],note='Keep the business names distinct. Grid orchestration is not proof of an LLM agent at Alabama Power. GE Aerospace’s disclosure concerns selected supply-chain functions, not utility dispatch.',takeaway='A real system needs both domain applications and a defined agent task.')
add('Industrial agents make the workflow visible', ['Siemens’ April 2026 Eigen Engineering Agent release names U.S. pilot customer Prism Systems.','The reported pattern is: assign a task, change automation code, validate, iterate, then engineer review.','This motivates tool use with observable tests, rather than accepting a generated answer alone.'],image='siemens_eigen.jpg',caption='Official Siemens Eigen Engineering Agent press visual, April 2026; promotional product imagery.',minutes=1.5,refs=['C09'],note='The official press visual illustrates the product; it is not a photograph of Prism’s deployment. Explain the Siemens source’s task-validation pattern. It is an engineering workflow, not evidence of live autonomous plant control.',takeaway='Task execution and checking are part of the system, not an afterthought.')
add('Read deployment claims by evidence type',table=[['Example','What is supported','What remains unproven'],['CAISO / OATI','Pilot plus supplier-reported production assistance','Independent causal reliability benefit'],['GE Vernova / Alabama Power','Operational platform deployment','LLM agentic control at the utility'],['GE Aerospace / Palantir','Selected agentic supply-chain deployment','Agent-specific quantified readiness gain'],['Siemens / Prism Systems','Named U.S. pilot customer; product launch','Universal productivity or field reliability'],['EPRI / Schneider','Research initiative / commercial product launch','A named U.S. autonomous utility-control outcome']],minutes=1.5,refs=['C01','C02','C05','C07','C09','C12','C14'],note='Use the evidence category rather than a marketing label. A customer, task and deployment status matter more than a framework logo. The full source guide carries the exact announcements and dates.',takeaway='Ask: which task, which tools, what result, and who decides?')
add('Frameworks: what each one provides',table=[['Framework','Main contribution','Engineering still required'],['LangGraph','Stateful graphs, checkpoints and interruptions','Case logic, policies and persistence setup'],['Microsoft Agent Framework','Agents and workflow orchestration','Identity and enterprise tool integration'],['OpenAI Agents SDK','Tools, handoffs and traces','Application limits and result validation'],['Google ADK','Agent construction, workflows and evaluation','Domain tools and a suitable test set'],['Harvard-led ToolUniverse','Scientific tool discovery and execution','Utility tools and utility-specific validation']],minutes=2,refs=['T01','T02','T04','T06','H01'],note='This is a map of reusable capabilities, not a ranking or a statement of utility readiness. Distinguish general development frameworks from a domain-oriented scientific research platform.',takeaway='The framework organizes work; the application supplies domain meaning.')
add('Harvard-led ToolUniverse', ['A Harvard Medical School-led team built an open platform for scientific agents.','It connects models to a library of scientific databases, software and simulators.','The lesson for utilities is a consistent, testable tool interface.'],image='framework_tooluniverse_ecosystem.png',caption='Original ToolUniverse ecosystem figure, Harvard Kempner Institute, 9 October 2025.',minutes=2,refs=['H01','H04','H05'],note='The current paper version reviewed is dated 7 August 2026. Avoid presenting the older figure’s historical tool count as today’s catalog size. This framework is scientific infrastructure, not a validated grid-control product.',takeaway='Domain tools turn a general model into a useful domain system.')
add('ToolUniverse: find a tool, then call it', ['Tool Finder identifies relevant capabilities; Tool Caller validates the request format and executes the structured call.','A utility application would need its own asset identities, units, permissions and engineering checks.'],image='framework_tooluniverse_protocol.png',caption='Original ToolUniverse Find Tool / Call Tool schematic, Harvard Kempner Institute.',kind='figure',minutes=1.5,refs=['H03','H05'],note='Read the four messages on the right: find tool, tool list, call tool, response. The protocol pattern is transferable; the scientific tool collection itself is not a utility operating model.',takeaway='Tool discovery and tool execution are distinct operations.')
add('POPPER: test a proposed explanation', ['POPPER is a Stanford–Harvard research collaboration published at ICML 2025.','It proposes falsification tests, executes analysis and combines statistical evidence.'],image='framework_popper_architecture.png',caption='Architecture portion of the authors’ POPPER figure. Full figure and paper are linked in the reading guide.',kind='figure',minutes=2,refs=['H09','H10','H11'],note='Harvard affiliation applies to co-author Ying Jin, not to every author. Explain the upper pipeline only. Its statistical guarantees depend on stated assumptions; they are not guarantees of electrical safety.',takeaway='Generate a candidate explanation, then seek evidence that could reject it.')
add('Frameworks can connect to existing agent interfaces', ['ToolUniverse shows integrations with Claude Desktop and Gemini CLI.', 'A utility application would still need scoped access, task state and a reviewable record.'],image='framework_tooluniverse_readme.png',caption='Original ToolUniverse README integration examples. Scientific-tool interfaces, not utility control software.',kind='figure',minutes=1.5,refs=['H04','T01'],note='This is an author-published integration example. Explain that the operator-facing application and the agent framework are different layers. The utility requirements are a proposed engineering transfer, not a claim about the pictured research interfaces.',takeaway='The operator uses an approved interface; the framework coordinates its tools.')
add('What transfers from research to utility work?',table=[['Research example','Reusable idea','Utility-specific addition'],['ToolUniverse','Find and call typed domain tools','Asset registry, telemetry and study adapters'],['TxAgent — Harvard-led biomedical research','Curated tools and evidence for a narrow domain','Approved procedures and engineering semantics'],['POPPER — Stanford–Harvard','Challenge a claim with explicit tests','Power-system constraints and model checks'],['Agent frameworks','State, routing and traceability','Operating authority and independent validation']],minutes=1.5,refs=['H01','H06','H07','H09','T01'],note='TxAgent is a separate therapeutic-reasoning research agent, not a clinical or utility deployment recommendation. These are design lessons. Domain transfer needs validation against the target task.',takeaway='Transfer the architecture and testing discipline; validate the new domain.')
add('New infrastructure for power-sector AI research', ['DOE CESER announced the LLNL Stormbreaker evaluation testbed in July 2026.','EPRI’s SAFERai.power initiative is developing risk and assessment guidance.','These efforts motivate domain-specific test environments and explicit operating scope.'],image='ornl_goal.jpg',caption='ORNL GOAL research laboratory. Context photo; this is not the LLNL Stormbreaker interface.',minutes=2.5,refs=['C15','C11','C12','I05'],note='Keep organizations distinct: LLNL develops the cited testbed; the photo is ORNL. The EPRI assessment effort is under development. Neither establishes certification of a particular utility agent.',takeaway='Evaluate the complete task in an appropriate domain environment.')
add('Evaluate actions and outcomes',table=[['Test','Evidence to inspect','Reason'],['Normal case','Correct result plus source links','Answer fluency is insufficient'],['Stale or missing data','Refresh request or explicit abstention','A current decision needs current evidence'],['Tool failure','Bounded retry and escalation','A failed computation is not a solved task'],['Malicious retrieved text','No unauthorized action','Tool content must not grant authority'],['Repeated runs','Success and failure rates with denominators','One demonstration is weak evidence']],minutes=1.5,refs=['T12','T14','C15'],note='tau2-bench studies coordinated agent/user tasks; AgentDojo studies injection in tool-returned content. They are research proxies, not grid certification. The table is a proposed local evaluation plan.',takeaway='Measure the behavior of the whole system, including the human review.')
add('Why this motivates GridGuard', ['Frameworks can coordinate a task, but they do not determine feeder feasibility.','GridGuard’s current prototype checks proposed actions with OpenDSS.','The research question is whether tool-guided proposals can become useful, traceable recommendations.'],image='gridguard_research_feeder.png',caption='Existing workshop figure: synthetic SMART-DS Greensboro feeder udt8894. Research-model context.',minutes=2,refs=['L01','L02'],note='The figure is a synthetic feeder, not a live utility circuit. The prototype accepts changes in simulation and does not command a live DMS. Do not introduce voltage results or switching experiments here; those belong to the separate use-case session.',takeaway='The motivation is useful proposals with explicit domain checks and evidence.')
add('The evidence an operator should receive',table=[['Part of the packet','What the operator can inspect'],['Context','Case, asset identity, data times and model version'],['Proposal','Exact target, units, intended effect and alternatives'],['Checks','Results, limits, assumptions and checks not performed'],['Decision record','Named reviewer, disposition and reason']],minutes=1,note='This is a proposed output contract. A reviewer needs observable evidence and a concise rationale, not hidden model chain-of-thought. A relevant change of state invalidates an outdated proposal.',takeaway='A recommendation is usable when its basis and limits are visible.')
add('Next tutorial: three worked use cases',table=[['Use case','Main question','Evidence to examine next'],['Voltage support','Can a candidate improve the operating state?','Feeder model, setpoints and constraint checks'],['Service restoration','Can switching restore service feasibly?','Topology, served load and switching constraints'],['Cyber response','How should uncertain information change the decision?','Data trust, quarantine and recovery evidence']],minutes=1,refs=['L02'],note='These names follow the existing workshop source. This slide previews the next tutorial; no worked numerical use case is taught in this introduction.',takeaway='Carry forward the same pattern: goal → tools → checks → operator review.')
add('Discussion and full readings', ['Which bounded task would you delegate first?','What evidence would make its output useful to an operator?','What result would make you stop or ask for fresh analysis?'],minutes=4,kind='closing',note='Reserve four minutes for discussion. End the main talk here. Open the separate Full Reading Guide for complete titles, authors, dates, original figures, paper PDFs, documentation and repositories. The nominal route totals 47 minutes; shorten discussion by two minutes for a 45-minute slot.',takeaway='Full Reading Guide: primary sources and direct links, organized by topic.')

